{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1885065146432688232', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjo4OTgzMjA5MjY=', 'rest_id': '898320926', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': False, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Mon Oct 22 20:15:03 +0000 2012', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': '#FlyEaglesFly Go Birds All in Tesla investor own M3P & Cybertruck MAGA MAHA - America First AF 1A 2A DOGE to the rescue 🚫No DM’s https://t.co/FHgydai4vv', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'ts.la/matthew78534', 'expanded_url': 'https://ts.la/matthew78534', 'url': 'https://t.co/FHgydai4vv', 'indices': [129, 152]}]}, 'url': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'ts.la/matthew78534', 'expanded_url': 'https://ts.la/matthew78534', 'url': 'https://t.co/FHgydai4vv', 'indices': [0, 23]}]}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 29441, 'followers_count': 5768, 'friends_count': 5521, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 8, 'location': 'Charleston, SC', 'media_count': 362, 'name': 'Matt', 'normal_followers_count': 5768, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1957467001086964153'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/898320926/1712640005', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1959364663445229568/JBAaRAu0_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'mmazechaz', 'statuses_count': 43372, 'translator_type': 'none', 'url': 'https://t.co/FHgydai4vv', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1885065146432688232'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1738273128000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '174', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/iphone" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPhone</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODUwNjUxNDYyMzEzMzI4NjQ=', 'text': 'Per GROK:\n\nScience is never truly "settled" because it is inherently based on the understanding that new evidence can always emerge to refine or even overturn existing theories. Here\'s why:\n\n- **Nature of Science**: Science progresses through the scientific method, which involves hypothesis testing, experimentation, observation, and peer review. Each step is designed to be provisional, allowing for revisions as new data or better interpretations come to light.\n\n- **Historical Examples**: \n  - **Heliocentrism**: The geocentric model was once considered settled science until Copernicus, Galileo, and others provided evidence for a heliocentric model.\n  - **Plate Tectonics**: The idea of continental drift was mocked until overwhelming evidence supported plate tectonics in the mid-20th century.\n  - **Physics**: Even foundational theories like Newtonian physics were later expanded by Einstein\'s theory of relativity, which itself is still being tested and refined.\n\n- **Current Research**: In fields like cosmology, biology, and physics, ongoing research frequently challenges or expands what was previously thought. For instance, the discovery of dark matter and dark energy has significantly altered our understanding of the universe.\n\n- **Philosophical Perspective**: From a philosophical standpoint, science aims at describing natural phenomena with the best explanation available at the time. Karl Popper\'s concept of falsifiability suggests that scientific theories are only scientific if they can potentially be proven wrong by new evidence.\n\n- **Scientific Consensus**: While there can be a strong scientific consensus on certain matters (like climate change or evolution), this consensus represents the current best understanding rather than an immutable truth. It\'s open to revision if compelling new evidence arises.\n\nIn conclusion, while there might be areas where science has reached a high level of agreement, describing science as "settled" can be misleading. Science thrives on curiosity, skepticism, and the pursuit of new knowledge, making it inherently dynamic and subject to change with new discoveries.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 30 20:38:48 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 1, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd Per GROK:\n\nScience is never truly "settled" because it is inherently based on the understanding that new evidence can always emerge to refine or even overturn existing theories. Here\'s why:\n\n- **Nature of Science**: Science progresses through the scientific method, which involves', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 0, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '898320926', 'id_str': '1885065146432688232'}}, '_legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 30 20:38:48 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 1, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@